lesson: 208
title: Eyes, ears and hands
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: Every person has 2 eyes, 2 ears and 2 hands, but only 1 nose.
explain: Teachers, parents and babies count too: a grown-up has 2 eyes just like a child.
explain: A class of 25 children with 2 teachers is 27 people, so it has 27 × 2 = 54 eyes.
vars: a=name b=name c=8..30 t=2..4
answer: 2 * (c + t)
exercise: A class has {c} children and {t} teachers. How many eyes are there in the classroom?
exercise: {c} children and {t} parents watch the school play. How many ears are listening?
exercise: At the end of the song, {c} children and {t} teachers clap. How many hands are clapping?
exercise: {a}'s class of {c} pupils goes to the museum with {t} adults. How many eyes look at the dinosaur?
exercise: How many hands go up when {c} children and their {t} coaches all raise both hands?
exercise: {c} kids + {t} teachers in the hall, how many eyes
exercise: {c} of us and {t} teachers, everyone clapping like mad. how many hands
exercise: there's {c+1} kids, nah {c}, {a}'s off sick, plus {t} teachers. ears?
exercise: {b} reckons {c} kids and {t} teachers have {c+t} eyes lol. how many eyes really
exercise: {c} children at the swimming gala with {t} helpers, and it was soooo loud. how many ears
exercise: we all put both hands up, {c} of us and {t} grown-ups. hands up total?
test: Count the eyes in a room where {t} teachers are marking and {c} children are reading.
test: {t} grown-ups lead {c} children through the forest, all holding hands with both hands. How many hands are there?
test: The audience was {c} pupils and {t} parents. How many ears heard the choir?
test: What is the number of eyes, if {c} children and {t} teachers watch a film and nobody has their eyes shut?
test: eyes on {c} kids n {t} teachers?
test: {t} teachers and {c} kids clapping, one kid dropped his lunch lol. hands?
exam: Determine the aggregate number of eyes possessed by a class of {c.words} pupils together with {t.words} teachers.
exam: It is given that an audience comprises {c} children and {t} adults. Ascertain the total quantity of ears present among the said audience.
exam: Whereas {c} pupils and {t} members of staff each raise both hands, compute the number of hands so raised.
exam: A party of {c} children, accompanied by {t} adults, visits a gallery. State the combined number of eyes belonging to the party.
exercise: A class has {c+1} children, but one is off with a tummy bug. With the {t} teachers, how many eyes are in the classroom?
exercise: {c} children and {t} teachers are in the room, and the head teacher has 'stepped out for a comfort break'. How many eyes are in the room?
test: {c} kids n {t} teachers, the head's 'in a meeting' (smoking out back lol). how many ears in the hall
